ll located in Evansville, Indiana, United States.","title":"Washington Square Mall (Evansville, Indiana)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It opened October 31, 1963 and was the first enclosed shopping center in Indiana.","title":"Washington Square Mall (Evansville, Indiana)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Developed by Erie Investments, the mall was originally anchored by Sears and an A & P supermarket.","title":"Washington Square Mall (Evansville, Indiana)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Louisville-based Stewart Dry Goods was added, as a second anchor department store, in 1969.","title":"Washington Square Mall (Evansville, Indiana)"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" This store -as well as the entire chain- was merged with Indianapolis' L. S. Ayres chain in 1980.","title":"Washington Square Mall (Evansville, Indiana)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Security Square Mall is a large mall in the suburbs of Baltimore, Maryland, United States.","title":"Security Square Mall"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The mall features over 100 stores and restaurants, as well as a food court, with Burlington Coat Factory, Macy's, Old Navy and Sears serving as anchor stores.","title":"Security Square Mall"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" One section of the mall, Seoul Plaza (formerly JCPenney), previously included Korean shops and restaurants; however, most of these establishments had closed by 2010.","title":"Security Square Mall"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Modell's Sporting Goods at Security closed down in late 2008 and now is a USA Discounters store.","title":"Security Square Mall"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Security Square Mall is located adjacent to the North American School of Trades.","title":"Security Square Mall"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"North Shore Square is a 621192 sqft shopping mall in Slidell, Louisiana.","title":"North Shore Square"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The mall is the largest mall on the Northshore of Lake Pontchartrain, fifth largest in the New Orleans area and the 11th largest in Louisiana.","title":"North Shore Square"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The mall is home to two anchor stores, Dillard's, and At Home, as well as approximately 23 other stores.","title":"North Shore Square"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" All the anchor stores are on one level.","title":"North Shore Square"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The mall did not flood during Hurricane Katrina and experienced no serious damage.","title":"North Shore Square"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" The mall formerly had Mervyns as an anchor store, but closed shortly after the storm when Mervyn's pulled out of the Louisiana market.","title":"North Shore Square"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" The store was eventually replaced by Burlington Coat Factory, which is now closed due to corporate downsizing.","title":"North Shore Square"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" JCPenney closed on July 31, 2017.","title":"North Shore Square"},{"sentence_id":8,"text":" The mall has struggled partially due to increased internet-based sales as well as an open-air shopping center located on the opposite side of town, to which it lost some of its tenants.","title":"North Shore Square"},{"sentence_id":9,"text":" Following a nationwide trend, the mall's future is uncertain as many former mall-based stores have either closed completely or downsized nationally, and enclosed shopping malls across the country are challenged by new consumer trends and shifting paradigms.","title":"North Shore Square"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Macy's
